# Wave W17-R (Route 125): ebb sand — tide-banded bay sand: a bright pale shore sand carrying its tide lines in the kind itself — darker wet bands standing across the tread where the ebb leaves its ruled marks, shore by shore (design: tide lines banding every shore of the Starfall north bay). Route 125’s own sand — the fleet’s only banded sand: split from Route 109’s unbanded bright gold by the tide lines themselves and from Route 124’s grey-wet crossing sand by brightness: this bay dries bright between tides.
